course: dictionary
lesson: 10752
title: Words that say how fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Urgently is an adverb. It tells you how something must be done: very quickly, because it matters and must happen right now. Look at the clues in this sentence: «A rabbit that stops eating or pooing for half a day needs a vet urgently.» The rabbit is in danger, so the vet must come fast.
explain: Notice where urgently sits in the sentence. It often comes at the end of a phrase, as in «needs a vet urgently» or «We need help urgently.» Ask yourself: must this happen right now? If yes, urgently fits.
explain: Urgent is an adjective (an urgent job), and urgently is the adverb that tells you how to do it (do it urgently). To check, swap in a word that means slowly, such as «needs a vet slowly». It makes no sense, so you know urgently means very quickly.
fact: Urgently means very quickly, because something is important and must be done right now.
fact: «We need help urgently.» means we need help at once, without waiting.
fact: In an emergency, call 999 (UK), 911 (US or Canada), 000 (Australia), 111 (New Zealand), or 112 or 999 (Ireland).
fact: Charities often say they urgently need donations or blood, because people in need cannot wait.
fact: Useful phrases: «urgently needed», «need something urgently», «speak urgently».
exercise: «A rabbit that stops eating needs a vet urgently.» What does urgently mean here? | Once a year, on a set day | *Very quickly, because it must be done right now | Quietly, so nobody hears | Slowly and carefully, over a long time
exercise: In Australia, which number do you call in an emergency? | 999 | *000 | 111 | 911
exercise: Which word is the adverb that means very quickly because it is urgent? | *Urgently | Urgency | Urging | Urgent
test: In a story, a character «speaks urgently» to a friend. What does this show? | The character is telling a joke | The character is very sleepy | The character is whispering a secret for fun | *The character is in danger or needs help right now
test: Charities say they «urgently need» blood. Why? | Because blood is cheap in the summer | Because the charity wants a party | Because blood is a type of food | *Because people need it now and cannot wait
exam: Which word best finishes this? The doctor said the patient needed an operation ___. | quietly | nicely | *urgently | yesterday
